 old but maybe  not as old as we  it's so this is the way to explain it  because obviously the tva is outside of  space and time right so i think he must  be very  hundreds and hundreds of years old  because time doesn't affect him in the  same way as it would  is as if if he was on earth  but my theory is and this is not like  this is just me guessing  i think we're i don't know i just think  i'm just trying to work it out really  because i feel like he  i think quite a few hundred years old  would be my guest because him and ren  slayer had this really beautiful deep  friendship and like i think everyone at  the tva is like  you know arguably they're all from the  beginning of time  because the timekeepers brought them  into existence so i think it's sort of  almost unknowable  for us to i mean i'm so bad at maths i  think it's almost unknowable for us to  work out how old he possibly could be  so it must be more than hundreds  actually so the first episode 50 minutes  second episode is 53 are the rest of the  episodes similar in length  yeah they kind of vary i think we we we  basically kind of did what was best for  the story  but they're all kind of around that  ballpark i would say more or less  sure i'm curious how it works though  with um  deleted scenes in a series like this do  you actually end up with a lot of stuff  on the cutting room floor and  if so is there any thought process about  how fans will eventually see it  sure um i think for i mean  it's like everything right there  definitely a scenes across the show that  we didn't end up putting in there just  because once you're in the edit right  like  when you're cutting sometimes there'll  be a scene where you're like oh actually  this is actually slowing the story down  and not pushing us forwards or  it you know sounds like tonally it  doesn't quite sit right so i think  that's just the nature of filmmaking so  in terms of the fan seeing any i guess  that would probably be more in marvel's  hands 